From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gureet <noreply@git.gureet.ca>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:53:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_audiotrack: pass E-AC-3, TrueHD and DTS-HD through

IEC 61937 has to go out at the rate and on the channels that the spdif
decoder sets for the format it carries: 192 kHz for E-AC-3 and DTS-HD,
and 8 channels for TrueHD and DTS-HD MA. ao_audiotrack capped every
stream at the native output rate and opened every passthrough track in
stereo, so these formats never matched and were decoded to PCM instead.

- Don't cap spdif formats at the native output rate.
- Open IEC 61937 with 8 channels as CHANNEL_OUT_7POINT1_SURROUND, and
  refuse other channel counts.
- Beyond 48 kHz stereo, ask AudioTrack.isDirectPlaybackSupported (API
  29 and later) first, and refuse when the output can't take it, so mpv
  falls back to PCM.

Dolby Digital and DTS at 48 kHz in stereo open as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c | 116 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 89 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

